<title>INDIA: India's Sona 96/97 net 93.7 mln rupees.</title>
<headline>India's Sona 96/97 net 93.7 mln rupees.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's Sona Steering Systems Ltd said on Wednesday that its net profit rose to 93.7 million rupees in 1996/97 (April-March) from 90.9 million in the previous financial year.  </p>
<p>Sona Steering, a joint venture between Maruti Udyog Ltd and Japan's Koyo Seiko Co Ltd, said the board of directors had recommended a dividend of 25 percent. It gave no comparative figure for 1995/96.</p>
<p>It said turnover rose to 1.53 billion rupees in 1996/97 from 1.27 billion in the previous financial year. The company's sales target for 1997/98 is 1.8 billion rupees, it said.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
